**Step 4: Create a controller method to handle file encryption**

```php
use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Storage;

class FileController extends Controller
{
    public function encryptFile(Request $request)
    {
        // Get the file from the request
        $file = $request->file('file');

        // Get the file extension
        $extension = $file->getClientOriginalExtension();

        // Generate a random encryption key
        $key = Str::random(32);

        // Create a new file name with the extension
        $fileName = "encrypted_" . $file->getClientOriginalName() . "." . $extension;

        // Encrypt the file and save it with the new name
        $file->storeAs($fileName, $key);

        // Return a success response
        return response()->json(['message' => 'File encrypted successfully']);
    }
}
```

